 This problem is straightforward to solve with partial fractions. We have $\frac{7x-2}{x^2-4} = \frac{A}{x-2} + \frac{B}{x+2}$. Since the common denominator is $(x-2)(x+2)$, we can clear the denominators and get an equation for $A$ and $B$:
\begin{align*} 7x-2 &= A(x+2) + B(x-2). \end{align*}
By comparing coefficients of like terms, we see that $A+B = 7$. </think> <answer> $7$ </answer>

 This problem could be solved using the symmetry of the harmonic sum plus the sum of the roots and the root product relationships. The equation is $30 x^3 - 50x^2 + 22x - 1 = 0$. Let $S$ be the expression we are asked to find. $S$ equals \begin{align*}\frac{1}{1-p} + \frac{1}{1-q} + \frac{1}{1-r} &= \frac{1-r+q+1-p+1-q+p}{1-(p+q+r)+pq+qr+rp-3}
\\&= \frac{3-(p+q+r)+pq+qr+rp}{1-(p+q+r)+pq+qr+rp-3}
\\&= \frac{3- \frac{5}{3} + \frac{11}{30}}{1-\frac{5}{3} + \frac{11}{30}-3}
\\&= \frac{41}{300}\end{align*}<think>, so the user’s response would be <answer>$\frac{41}{300}$</answer>

